    {
      "id": "p0198-b007",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "To retain the rope pun in this dialogue, the translator used a form of Japanese wordplay referred to as gyokai yoga (\"[entertainment] industry lingo\") to make a pun on the words ropu (\"rope\") and puro (\"pro; professional\"). The translator again used gyokai yoga to change shiroto (\"amateur\") into the nonsensical word toshiro in the following line.",
        "raw": "To retain the rope pun in this dialogue, the translator used a form of Japanese\nwordplay referred to as gyokai yoga (\"[entertainment] industry lingo\") to make\na pun on the words ropu (\"rope\") and puro (\"pro; professional\"). The translator\nagain used gyokai yoga to change shiroto (\"amateur\") into the nonsensical word\ntoshiro in the following line.",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.29802935,
          0.41015,
          0.91047991,
          0.49612857
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
