    {
      "id": "p0198-b011",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In simple terms, Japanese gyokai yoga, sometimes referred to as zujago, is similar to English \"Pig Latin\" -you basically shuffle and move the characters in a word to create a new, funny-sounding \"secret code word\".",
        "raw": "In simple terms, Japanese gyokai yoga, sometimes referred to as zujago,\nis similar to English \"Pig Latin\" -you basically shuffle and move the\ncharacters in a word to create a new, funny-sounding \"secret code word\".",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en"
        ],
        "bbox": [
          0.32745904,
          0.75076429,
          0.88479284,
          0.79620714
        ],
        "mask_bbox": [
          0.32612969,
          0.75005,
          0.88612218,
          0.79727857
        ],
        "line_ids": [
          46,
          47,
          48
        ]
      },
      "translation": {
        "text": "简单说，这种行话有时也叫 zūjago，类似英语的 Pig Latin（儿童黑话）：调换词内字符，造出一个听起来好笑的新“暗号词”。",
        "status": "draft",
