    {
      "id": "p0198-b012",
      "kind": "paragraph",
      "source": {
        "text": "In basic gyōkai yōgo, the final character in a word is moved to the front, and certain vowels are elongated. For example, トマト (tomato) might become トートマ (tōtoma), while スシ (sushi) might become シースー (shīsū).",
        "raw": "In basic gyokai yogo, the final character in a word is moved to the front,\nand certain vowels are elongated. For example, 1--~ 1-- (tomato) might\nbecome f..-1--~ (totoma), while ;z~ (sushi) might become ~-;z- (shTsO).",
        "status": "corrected",
        "languages": [
          "en",
          "ja"
        ],
        "bbox": [
